   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Root Hair Cells"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- Root hairs cells are found in the epidermis of plant roots\n- These specialised cells have extensions known as **root hairs** that grow in between soil particles\n- Root hairs** increase the surface area** of the epidermal cells, **aiding absorption of water and mineral ions** from the soil"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2020/01/Structure-of-the-root.png",
   "file": "assets/46844b5d3f01-structure-of-the-root.png",
   "alt": "Structure of the root, IGCSE & GCSE Biology revision notes",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "***Root hair cells are found around the outside of plant roots where they aid absorption of water and minerals from the soil***"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "Identifying root hair cells"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- Root hair cells can be **identified **by their root hairs which extend from the surface of the root epidermis"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2024/05/800px-monocot-root-epidermal-root-hair-in-lilium-36045152715.jpg",
